                    Preamble

  The TimWorks Engine Public License (TWEPL) is intended
to provide users with the freedom to use, study, modify,
and redistribute TimWorks Engine.

  This license permits both personal and commercial use of the
Engine. Users may modify the Engine, maintain private forks, and 
redistribute original or modified versions without being required 
to publish or disclose their modified source code.

  Redistributions must preserve the applicable copyright notices and
a copy of this license, ensuring that the original terms governing
the Engine remain identifiable.

  TWEPL is designed to encourage experimentation, independent
development, and the creation of derivative projects while allowing 
developers to decide whether their own modifications remain private 
or are shared with the community.

  This license applies only to materials covered by it. Third-party
components remain subject to their respective licenses.

                 1. Definitions

      For the purposes of this license, the following
       terms shall have the meanings set forth below.

  1.1 "TimWorks Engine"

  "TimWorks Engine" or the "Original Engine" refers to the original
software project known as TimWorks Engine, including its engine source
code, libraries, build tools, documentation, and other materials
distributed under this license by the applicable Copyright Holder.

  1.2 "Software"

  "Software" refers to any portion of TimWorks Engine that is made
available under this license, including source code, compiled binaries,
libraries, tools, and accompanying documentation.

  1.3 "Copyright Holder"

  "Copyright Holder" refers to the person or legal entity that owns the
copyright in the relevant portion of the Software.

  1.4 "License"

  "License" refers to the TimWorks Engine Public License (TWEPL),
including the applicable version identified in the accompanying license
notice.

  1.5 "Licensee"

  "Licensee" refers to any individual, organization, or legal entity
exercising rights granted under this license.

  1.6 "Modification"

  "Modification" refers to any alteration, adaptation, improvement,
removal, replacement, or extension of the original Engine's source
code or other covered components.
  Examples include changes to rendering, audio, input handling,
platform support, engine architecture, build systems, and other
Engine functionality.

  1.7 "Modified Version"

  "Modified Version" refers to a version of TimWorks Engine that
contains one or more Modifications to the original Engine.
  A Modified Version may be maintained privately, distributed
publicly, distributed commercially, or incorporated into another
software product, subject to the terms of this license.

  1.8 "Fork"

  "Fork" refers to an independent continuation, copy, or derivative
development branch of TimWorks Engine maintained separately from
the original project.
  A Fork may use the TimWorks Engine name or a different name,
subject to applicable trademark rights and the other terms of
this license.

  1.9 "Redistribution"

  "Redistribution" refers to providing, transmitting, publishing,
selling, sublicensing where permitted, or otherwise making a copy
of the Software or a Modified Version available to another person
or entity.
  Redistribution includes distribution through websites, software
repositories, digital storefronts, physical media, downloadable
packages, and other distribution channels.

  1.10 "Game or Application Using the Engine"

  "Game or Application Using the Engine" refers to a game,
application, or other software product that incorporates, links
to, bundles, or is distributed with TimWorks Engine or a
Modified Version of it.
  This term includes products distributed in compiled form,
whether or not the Engine's source code is included.

  1.11 "Attribution Notice"

  "Attribution Notice" refers to a notice identifying 
TimWorks Engine as the original Engine and, where applicable,
identifying the Engine version, the name of the Fork, and the
relationship between the two projects.

  1.12 "Modification Disclosure"

  "Modification Disclosure" refers to a reasonable written
summary of material changes made to the original Engine, as
required by this license.
  A Modification Disclosure describes the nature of the changes
but does not, by itself, require disclosure of source code, private
repositories, or proprietary implementation details.

  1.13 "Source Code"

  "Source Code" refers to the preferred form of a work for making
modifications, including human-readable source files, build scripts,
configuration files, and other materials needed to modify the
relevant Software.

  1.14 "Object Code"

  "Object Code" refers to a compiled or otherwise machine-readable
form of the Software that is not presented in its preferred
human-readable form for modification.

  1.15 "Third-Party Component"

  "Third-Party Component" refers to any software, library, asset,
tool, or other material included with or used by TimWorks Engine that
is owned by another party or distributed under separate license terms.
  Third-Party Components remain subject to their applicable licenses.

      2. Fork Attribution and Modification Disclosure

  2.1 Attribution Requirement

  Any person or entity that redistributes the Engine, a Modified Version
of the Engine, or a Game or Application Using the Engine that
incorporates a Modified Version must provide an Attribution Notice
identifying TimWorks Engine as the original Engine.
  The notice must identify the original Engine version on which the
Modified Version is based, where reasonably ascertainable, and the name
of the Fork or Modified Version, if one has been assigned.

  2.2 Modification Disclosure

  Any person or entity that redistributes a Modified Version of the 
Engine, or a Game or Application Using the Engine that incorporates a
Modified Version, must provide a reasonable written summary of the
material modifications made to the Engine.
  The disclosure must describe significant changes to the Engine,
including applicable changes to rendering, audio, input handling,
platform support, engine architecture, build systems, or other
major functionality.
  To the extent reasonably known, the disclosure should also
identify material modifications inherited from an existing Fork.
  This requirement does not require disclosure of source code,
private repositories, proprietary implementation details, or
modifications unrelated to the Engine. A redistributor is not
required to disclose information that they do not reasonably
know and cannot reasonably determine.

  2.3 Placement of Notices

  The Attribution Notice and Modification Disclosure must accompany
each distributed release in a reasonably accessible location
appropriate to the distribution method.

    Acceptable locations include:
  - A README, NOTICE, or credits file supplied with the release.
  - An About, Credits, or Legal Notices screen within a distributed
      game or application.
  - The product or download page through which the release is distributed.
  - Documentation or other materials supplied with a physical or
      digital release.

  The notice must be reasonably accessible to recipients of the
distributed product. Merely keeping the notice in a private repository
or internal development document does not satisfy this requirement.
  For products distributed through multiple channels, the notice must
be made available through each channel, either directly or through
materials accompanying the distribution.
Where a game incorporates a Modified Version of the Engine, the
notice may appear in the game's credits or other appropriate in-game
or accompanying materials.

  2.4 Example Attribution

  A compliant notice may use the following format:
"This product uses a fork of TimWorks Engine 0.1 called GoldWorks.
GoldWorks is an independently developed modification of TimWorks Engine.
  Engine modifications: Replaced the rendering backend, modified input
handling, and added support for additional platforms.
  TimWorks Engine and its original Copyright Holder do not necessarily
endorse, maintain, or support GoldWorks."
  Redistributors must replace the example details with accurate
information about their own product and the modifications made
to the Engine.

  2.5 No Source Publication Requirement

  Compliance with this section requires attribution and a reasonable
description of material Engine modifications only. Nothing in this
section requires the publication or disclosure of modified source
code, private development materials, proprietary implementation
details, or internal repositories.

  2.6 No Implied Endorsement

  Attribution under this section does not imply that TimWorks Engine
or its original Copyright Holder endorses, maintains, or supports any
Fork, game, application, or derivative project.

